Bugfix: A login without user name no longer logs a PHP deprecation

A login form sent without the user or password field, or with one of them as a
list (user[]=x), reached the password check with null. PHP then logged
"Passing null to parameter" from str_replace() for each of them. A missing
field now counts as empty. A list as user name or password is refused before
the brute force throttle or a user backend sees it. The login still fails with
"Wrong password".
